{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr","id":1181695,"title":"Why is there no dingo/out of asia foxes/out of europe Apis/Grondr","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-02T10:07:54-08:00","id":1181695,"title":"Why is there no dingo/out of asia foxes/out of europe Apis/Grondr","content":"So I was going to complain about the idiocy of Australia, in the world of darkness of course (all other australian idiocies can go elsewhere) and the use of Tas tigers for garou rather those ubiquitous dingos (I'm sure it's metaphoric for the eradication of Aborigines, but you could do something <i>smarter</i> )but then I thought &quot;hold on a moment, there's wild and mighty bovines just about everywhere outside of europe, as there are wild bacon counterparts, why are these two breeds extinct? Then we have foxes, and I don't think I really need much to say about those, they're tricksters everywhere, but some anime loving fool decided to keep the changers in east asia and stick them with the Japanese name. Now I understand that japan has a disproportionate cultural impact on the west relative to the rest of asia, and their industry grabbed the US, but any broader understanding of east asian history just makes it seem <i>wrong</i>. <br /> <br /> Then I realise there's no clever subtext or anything to look into here, from the ground up, some changing breeds have been <i>really shallow. </i>Horrendously ill thought out, someone sucks with geography, mythology or taxonomy, and the only methods'll be to fix the wars of rage so that <i>everything </i>ate the bacon and the beef and the foxes out of asia, that australia systematically killed all the dingo tribe that nobody heard of,despite the success of the species (the Thylacin gets a few more cave paintings and had the merit of being killed off by <i>europeans </i>which is nice for white-guilt drama but it's pretty clear what the <i>logical </i>choice for australia was. I mean they could've had both, but if it's one or the other, no way the garou wouldn't be dingos) <br /> <br /> So, a re-tread into forgotten parts of the Rage wars would make a lot of sense. The Garou get too much flak for genocide, when really I think they were just the best suited for it by luck (coincidentally, Europeans get the most flak for colonialism,slavery and genocide because their advantages in geography, resulting technology and such made them the <i>best</i> at it, and had another continent got that leg up instead, the world'd have a <i>different </i>oppressor with a <i>different </i>race on top, because <i>every </i>continent had their share of people fond of that sort of thing, they just don't get so much flak because they were less successful. If we run by that logic, then maybe the Bastet could've been the primary antagonist with a less successful wolf.) Disclaimer: I'm not saying the europeans weren't horrible and we should all be insensitive to all those who suffered, I'm saying everyone's horrible, or at least the people in power are. Just making it clear. <br /> <br /> The other tactic, of course, would be to straight up retcon everything awful. Write the dingos in, the boars and bovines of the Americas and Africas, the foxes of everywhere. But as we're 20 years into this, maybe it's a bit late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:39:27-08:00","id":1181730,"title":"","content":"There are Dingos, most Australian born Lupus Garou are born of them. They aren't part of the Bunyip because Dingos didn't appear on the continent until much later.<br /> <br /> Non-Asian kitsune don't appear because the breed is young and they draw their root from the Far East. They have taken part almost exclusively in the Beast Courts til now. Their breeding issues also makes expansion very difficult. <br /> <br /> No excuse on the last point. Their are still true wild Boars/Wart Hogs and Bovine to this day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:54:55-08:00","id":1181741,"title":"","content":"As Derhuzad said for the Bunyip and Kitsune. <br /> <br /> Regards the Gondr, Apis they are dead in the same way the Camasotz are dead. War or Rage species killing in Fera Ancient-Pre History has done the damage on both the physical and spiritual level to remove the Changing Breed entirely. Actually there are some &quot;Grondr&quot; still around, what's left of them are the Wyrm Monsters known as SkullPigs, the Apis is dead, dead but the Camasotz also have some dodgy Wyrmy echoes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T12:07:52-08:00","id":1181746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1181730#post1181730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-Asian kitsune don't appear because the breed is young and they draw their root from the Far East. They have taken part almost exclusively in the Beast Courts til now. Their breeding issues also makes expansion very difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the stupid part though. <i>why </i>do they draw their root from the far east, with all the fox tricksters in existence (and if it was for the whole nine-tailed thing, that could've been a totem, and one could've had the wits to recognise that the japanese borrowed the myth) when the red fox spans the entirity of the northern hemisphere and<i> the east asian myths aren't even the best ones</i>. Someone just went &quot;oh this sounds so exotic&quot; when they've probably got a fox within a few miles of em. Why are they new? Why have they just chosen asia despite everything. The only answer is <i>writers, </i>and that's never a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T12:10:33-08:00","id":1181747,"title":"","content":"These were just design choices the original developers made. If you don't like them, change them in your chronicles.<br /> <br /> I never accepted the idea that marsupial predators were wolves, so I've never considered the Bunyip to be Garou. They are simply another Changing Breed. Everything else remain the same - the Garou still wiped them out and then felt guilty about it. I've never had anyone in my games which objected to that.<br /> <br /> In Rage Across Australia, they had Red Talons have the forms of dingoes and in other sourcebooks they've taken the form of Painted Hunting Dogs (in Africa). I've always been leery on this, as once you have Garou assuming non-wolf forms, I think it can create a lot of problems. If Garou can take those forms, why can't Bone Gnawers take the form of at least some dogs? Why are Nuwisha separate from Garou? I think a hard line has to be drawn somewhere so it is coherent, reasonable, and prevents ridiculousness. That line will be different for different people.<br /> <br /> They made werefoxes Asian only because it is really only in China and Japan that have myths of werefoxes (or foxwomen actually). There isn't a tradition of people who turn into foxes (or vice versa) in Europe or elsewhere. So it actually makes sense they don't exist elsewhere. Still, I like my tales of Reynard the Fox as well so there is no reason why the occasional werefox can't show up elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where the Apis and Grondr comment comes from because they were exterminated everywhere in the Old World. Aurochs were never in Australia or the New World nor were Boars (at least not until the Columbian Exchange). As to why small pockets of them did not survive in areas where wolves are not naturally present, there can be lots of reasonable explanations. Kinfolk for those creatures need not be equally distributed everywhere. Garou can follow moon bridges and travel to lots of places. And I've always held that the &quot;War of Rage&quot; was not a real event, but a historical term developed long after that time to give narrative and explanation for a long series of conflicts (in the same sense that historians created the Hundred Years War to cover a series of similar, but quite distinct separate wars). The other werecreatures butchered each other just as much as the Garou did so if there were some Apis surviving in Africa, the Simba and Ajaba probably killed them for the same reason the Garou killed them in their lands - they were local competitors and got in the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 02-03-2018, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:03:28-08:00","id":1181765,"title":"","content":"Basically?<br /> <br /> The original material was written with sounds &quot;cool at the time&quot; beating, &quot;hey should we consider this in more detail?&quot; And there was a refusal to do anything but minor retcons over time to address this.<br /> <br /> The setting is illogical in hindsight, because it wasn't trying to be coherently logical in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T14:24:58-08:00","id":1181800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1181765#post1181765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically?<br /> <br /> The original material was written with sounds &quot;cool at the time&quot; beating, &quot;hey should we consider this in more detail?&quot; And there was a refusal to do anything but minor retcons over time to address this.<br /> <br /> The setting is illogical in hindsight, because it wasn't trying to be coherently logical in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. There's logic to satire even when it's a farce. Some of werewolf <i>really </i>makes sense in a dumb way, not nearly as much as vampire, but it's enough to make you think. This is one of my favourite things about WoD, and when it's absent and just dumb without that sense, the quality is less, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Though you know that chinatown part of the endgame for the bloodlines game where everyone's dressed in colour coded MA uniforms and most are using knives or crossbows, there's bamboo traps and people come out of walls? That was incredibly dumb, but they knew it, and it made sense in a camp and stupid way, and I'm not sure if it was excellent because they <i>knew</i> it was dumb (not the level design though, that was a pretty shit level)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":23728,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","user":"PewPew","date":". 02-02-2018, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T14:48:31-08:00","id":1181810,"title":"","content":"The games aren't meant to be satire or farce. They're not intended to be overtly comedic in their approach to commentary. It's supposed to make you think via the punk side of the themes being in your face and dramatic, rather than mockery.<br /> <br /> VtM: Bloodlines was put out in 2004, clearly recognizing some of the inherently silly things in the WoD and running with them as part of the aesthetic. It reflects the games well, but doesn't really say much about why these things were created the way they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T19:18:11-08:00","id":1181887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr#post1181695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was going to complain about the idiocy of Australia, in the world of darkness of course (all other australian idiocies can go elsewhere) and the use of Tas tigers for garou rather those ubiquitous dingos (I'm sure it's metaphoric for the eradication of Aborigines, but you could do something <i>smarter</i> )but then I thought &quot;hold on a moment, there's wild and mighty bovines just about everywhere outside of europe, as there are wild bacon counterparts, why are these two breeds extinct? Then we have foxes, and I don't think I really need much to say about those, they're tricksters everywhere, but some anime loving fool decided to keep the changers in east asia and stick them with the Japanese name. Now I understand that japan has a disproportionate cultural impact on the west relative to the rest of asia, and their industry grabbed the US, but any broader understanding of east asian history just makes it seem <i>wrong</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anime? No, OA, as in the AD&amp;D book. The creators of the WoD are rpg players from an older generation, and that was what a lot of them got into the hobby playing. This is also why some stuff from D&amp;D got carried over without much questioning, like the presentation of Tou Mu, or the completely fabricated demon archer (the fact that it's made up is not nearly so bad as the fact that it was made up by someone else and suggests that, much like in the works of the webcomic creator Krazy Krow, D&amp;D books of early vintage are genuine occult texts)..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then I realise there's no clever subtext or anything to look into here, from the ground up, some changing breeds have been <i>really shallow. </i>Horrendously ill thought out, someone sucks with geography, mythology or taxonomy, and the only methods'll be to fix the wars of rage so that <i>everything </i>ate the bacon and the beef and the foxes out of asia, that australia systematically killed all the dingo tribe that nobody heard of,despite the success of the species (the Thylacin gets a few more cave paintings and had the merit of being killed off by <i>europeans </i>which is nice for white-guilt drama but it's pretty clear what the <i>logical </i>choice for australia was. I mean they could've had both, but if it's one or the other, no way the garou wouldn't be dingos)<br /> <br /> So, a re-tread into forgotten parts of the Rage wars would make a lot of sense. The Garou get too much flak for genocide, when really I think they were just the best suited for it by luck (coincidentally, <b>Europeans get the most flak for colonialism,slavery and genocide because their advantages in geography, resulting technology and such made them the <i>best</i> at it, and had another continent got that leg up instead, the world'd have a <i>different </i>oppressor with a <i>different </i>race on top, because <i>every </i>continent had their share of people fond of that sort of thing,</b> they just don't get so much flak because they were less successful. If we run by that logic, then maybe the Bastet could've been the primary antagonist with a less successful wolf.) Disclaimer: I'm not saying the europeans weren't horrible and we should all be insensitive to all those who suffered, I'm saying everyone's horrible, or at least the people in power are. Just making it clear.<br /> <br /> The other tactic, of course, would be to straight up retcon everything awful. Write the dingos in, the boars and bovines of the Americas and Africas, the foxes of everywhere. But as we're 20 years into this, maybe it's a bit late. </div> </div> </div>&quot;If I didn't do it, someone else would have!&quot; never wins you many friends in debate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T03:11:59-08:00","id":1181956,"title":"","content":"RE: Kitsune<br /> <br /> They are focused as such because they came about in the Hengyokai book during the year of the Lotus late 2nd edition and were not a part of the Werewolf cosmology until then. Any of the Western type Fox-Shifter-Tricksters would be Pooka from Changeling the Dreaming. The Kistune legends have a slightly different flavour to them than the fox legends and myths in the west and as such they worked quite well for the Year of the Lotus to have a different Changing breed from everything done before up to that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T09:48:20-08:00","id":1182017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1181810#post1181810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The games aren't meant to be satire or farce. They're not intended to be overtly comedic in their approach to commentary. It's supposed to make you think via the punk side of the themes being in your face and dramatic, rather than mockery.<br /> <br /> VtM: Bloodlines was put out in 2004, clearly recognizing some of the inherently silly things in the WoD and running with them as part of the aesthetic. It reflects the games well, but doesn't really say much about why these things were created the way they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, minus the Society of Leopold mission, most of the end missions in Bloodlines were very awkward combat/stealth levels that were clearly a bit rushed. You could talk your way out of stuff in previous levels atleast in parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T10:02:44-08:00","id":1182018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1181956#post1181956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: Kitsune<br /> <br /> They are focused as such because they came about in the Hengyokai book during the year of the Lotus late 2nd edition and were not a part of the Werewolf cosmology until then. Any of the Western type Fox-Shifter-Tricksters would be Pooka from Changeling the Dreaming. The Kistune legends have a slightly different flavour to them than the fox legends and myths in the west and as such they worked quite well for the Year of the Lotus to have a different Changing breed from everything done before up to that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kitsune first showed up in Caerns: Places of Power from 1993 and is a first edition sourcebook.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T19:59:07-08:00","id":1182156,"title":"","content":"I'd just have the Bunyip mate with Dingoes. Solves the problem.<br /> <br /> But in many myths dogs, coyotes, and wolves are spiritually distinct animals. You can see this reflected in the Changing Breeds to a degree, but Apocalypse IMO suffered from the early developers not emphasizing enough on how Werebeasts are half spirit, half flesh creatures. Part of their very make up is the symbolism of the animal they shift into, and why no random Croatan or Bunyip descended Garou, or the extinct species of Fera are ever going to ever be born again; the spirit half is gone forever. This was something I felt was better emphasized right off the bat in Forsaken, which avoided things like the 'Garou gene' that later had to be retconned (despite the DNA company still being a thing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T20:30:38-08:00","id":1182161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1182156#post1182156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just have the Bunyip mate with Dingoes. Solves the problem.<br /> <br /> But in many myths dogs, coyotes, and wolves are spiritually distinct animals. You can see this reflected in the Changing Breeds to a degree, but Apocalypse IMO suffered from the early developers not emphasizing enough on how Werebeasts are half spirit, half flesh creatures. Part of their very make up is the symbolism of the animal they shift into, and why no random Croatan or Bunyip descended Garou, or the extinct species of Fera are ever going to ever be born again; the spirit half is gone forever. This was something I felt was better emphasized right off the bat in Forsaken, which avoided things like the 'Garou gene' that later had to be retconned (despite the DNA company still being a thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised (and W20, presumably before KABA) had DNA hitting their heads against a brick wall because they couldn't explain how anything about the Garou worked, and their theoretical framework for trying was a nightmarish doorstopper's doorstopper of notebooks awash in caffeine and delusion. This could have been further driven home, to be sure (keeping them from even identifying Kinfolk through gene markers), but we seem to have been forced back to square one because of ParaWolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T20:35:50-08:00","id":1182164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1181746#post1181746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the stupid part though. <i>why </i>do they draw their root from the far east, with all the fox tricksters in existence (and if it was for the whole nine-tailed thing, that could've been a totem, and one could've had the wits to recognise that the japanese borrowed the myth) when the red fox spans the entirity of the northern hemisphere and<i> the east asian myths aren't even the best ones</i>. Someone just went &quot;oh this sounds so exotic&quot; when they've probably got a fox within a few miles of em. Why are they new? Why have they just chosen asia despite everything. The only answer is <i>writers, </i>and that's never a good one.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are tricksters, but foxes as shapeshifting spirit-creatures is pretty culturally distinct; and that was the lore they built the Kitsune Gifts et all around.<br /> <br /> Also WtA Kitsune aren't inherently tricksters (though many chose to be). That's the Nuwisha's bag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T03:22:52-08:00","id":1182212,"title":"","content":"OMG, this blog has really jumped out at me today.<br /> <br /> First I am with Black Fox, World of Darkness was very welcoming to new freelance writers and I loved this game because they expected the content of their customers! so if there is a whole in &quot;Logic&quot; for what animals &quot;should be&quot; Werebeast or &quot;Where&quot; they should be. I say do it make a story or chronical in that area get some players and run the Dingo tribes of Australia, Boar of the Bayau - Gondr of the Mississippi Delta, or Red Barons the Foxes of Europe.<br /> <br /> I know for Hengeyokai book (page 149) Brings up Fox kin being many places. I was thinking of running some games and making a Submission about Foxes of the world! Come up with tribes and sects. <br /> <br /> It is my thoughts that White Wolf didn't &quot;Do it wrong&quot;, The opened a door for personal creativity and that is why we have all these people here<br /> <br /> I was working a Noah's Ark project for a few years looking for different shifters and books and supporting data!<br /> <br /> Thank you for new inspiration!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T06:25:35-08:00","id":1182241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1182161#post1182161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Revised (and W20, presumably before KABA) had DNA hitting their heads against a brick wall because they couldn't explain how anything about the Garou worked, and their theoretical framework for trying was a nightmarish doorstopper's doorstopper of notebooks awash in caffeine and delusion. This could have been further driven home, to be sure (keeping them from even identifying Kinfolk through gene markers), but we seem to have been forced back to square one because of ParaWolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the Parawolf and the other Pentex created werebeasts made me want to hit my head against the wall in regards to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-04-2018, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T10:21:57-08:00","id":1182306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1182241#post1182241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah the Parawolf and the other Pentex created werebeasts made me want to hit my head against the wall in regards to this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe by &quot;ParaWolf&quot;, Saur Ops Specialist was referring to Paradox/White Wolf.<br /> <br /> The Mockeries only work because they're actually using Wyrm magic, it's not actual genetic science, which is why D.N.A. wasn't able to do anything with the same data.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T11:00:04-08:00","id":1182317,"title":"","content":"I have no problem with there being some kind of genetic component to Garou. After all, while they may be part spirit, their kinfolk aren't. Yet mating with kinfolk leads to different results than mating with humans. That there is some kind of special biology distinguishing them seems to be OK. However, the genetic component alone should be useless without the spiritual component which is what provides all the actual powers to the Garou. (And it may even be possible that monkeying around with that biology somehow taints the person and blocks the spiritual component from doing its thing).<br /> <br /> And I also don't mind that researching whatever this biological component is might lead to certain benefits. In my chronicles, DNA has created various treatments for very rare genetic diseases as a result of their research into lycanthropes. It hasn't allowed them to create superpowers though. They are treading onto forbidden ground though, and it is entirely possible their research could lead to something very bad happening. But if it does, it'll fall into the realm of science horror that obeys the laws of physics rather than supernatural horror which ignores them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T12:15:24-08:00","id":1182345,"title":"","content":"I think the mockery breeds are some of the coolest things ever, and I've always wanted my very own warwolf playing as the other splats. The cockroaches only really work in a horror type deal, there are so many more effective creatures for an assassin type breed, whilst the rhino's more of a deadly joke that's somehow more stupid than the rokea (whom I love) but the frogs will some day be a success. They WILL BE A SUCCESS. Freakfeet, whilst a failure from the point of view that they couldn't be controlled, are a fantastic distraction for pentex, but the mockery breed... They can only get better. <br /> <br /> I mean a frog is a poor choice for seawater, what were they thinking, but that's workable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T14:18:34-08:00","id":1182382,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve decided at my own table, Eterent, a Pentex agribusiness at the forefront of deforestation of the Amazon, has pulled off the ultimate perversion in the eyes of the Fera: they\u2019ve bred Mockeries of the Apis and Grondr on their ranches and pig farms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-04-2018, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T18:19:43-08:00","id":1182458,"title":"","content":"I don't care for the Mockery breeds. It goes against the Wyrm's nature and theme of being a corrupter and destroyer of things that already exist. Creating new things violates this IMO. I'm also not a fan of a lot of pseudo-science explanation for stuff anymore. It also leads to those awkward questions of why the Garou can't breed with dogs or coyotes, etc.<br /> <br /> Each to their own though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-04-2018, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T20:12:00-08:00","id":1184597,"title":"","content":"Apis and Grondr became extinct before they spread their culture across all of humanity, though I have issues about Camazotz being wiped out so late...<br /> <br /> And I like to have Kitsune have started to spread out to foreign foxes, like Ajaba started their diaspora.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T23:30:33-08:00","id":1184648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1181887#post1181887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anime? No, OA, as in the AD&amp;D book. The creators of the WoD are rpg players from an older generation, and that was what a lot of them got into the hobby playing. This is also why some stuff from D&amp;D got carried over without much questioning, like the presentation of Tou Mu, or the completely fabricated demon archer (the fact that it's made up is not nearly so bad as the fact that it was made up by someone else and suggests that, much like in the works of the webcomic creator Krazy Krow, D&amp;D books of early vintage are genuine occult texts)..</div> </div> </div> </div>Who or what is the demon archer that you mentioned? Where can I read about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T01:29:53-08:00","id":1184660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1182156#post1182156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just have the Bunyip mate with Dingoes. Solves the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately it doesn\u2019t solve any problem. The Bunyip tribe would have been long extinct for thousands of years before the dingo even showed up.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve no doubt that the original Werewolf writers included the Bunyip/Thylacine thing simply because they saw these things that were sometimes called wolves and decided \u2018this would be cool\u2019. We tried to reconcile that it did exist with why it did so in Shattered Dreams, but you know...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T01:52:58-08:00","id":1184665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1184660#post1184660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately it doesn\u2019t solve any problem. The Bunyip tribe would have been long extinct for thousands of years before the dingo even showed up.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve no doubt that the original Werewolf writers included the Bunyip/Thylacine thing simply because they saw these things that were sometimes called wolves and decided \u2018this would be cool\u2019. We tried to reconcile that it did exist with why it did so in Shattered Dreams, but you know...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've always been confused about the tribe wolf blood thing, especially in light of how its an issue for the Hakken who may have lost their Wolf stock as recently as last century but never was a issue for the Fianna where it looks like the last wolf in the British isles was in the 16th century.<br /> <br /> and a Lupus focused contingent forcing their way into new lands and breeding with the previously unused human stock would sort of neatly match up with the history of the Dingo's introduction to Australia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T13:13:05-08:00","id":1184855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1184648#post1184648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who or what is the demon archer that you mentioned? Where can I read about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chih-chiang Fyu-ya, who exists in AD&amp;D 1e (see Deities and Demigods p 38), KotE (main book p 213), and nowhere in Chinese folklore that's turned up over the past few years that I've been looking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T10:52:01-08:00","id":1185649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1184660#post1184660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately it doesn\u2019t solve any problem. The Bunyip tribe would have been long extinct for thousands of years before the dingo even showed up.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve no doubt that the original Werewolf writers included the Bunyip/Thylacine thing simply because they saw these things that were sometimes called wolves and decided \u2018this would be cool\u2019. We tried to reconcile that it did exist with why it did so in Shattered Dreams, but you know...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Dingo could have arrived to Australia anywhere between 3,500 to 12,000 years ago. Going at the higher end of that range would coincide with the Bunyip's arrival to Australia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1184665#post1184665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've always been confused about the tribe wolf blood thing, especially in light of how its an issue for the Hakken who may have lost their Wolf stock as recently as last century but never was a issue for the Fianna where it looks like the last wolf in the British isles was in the 16th century.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could expand the Hakken's kin range to the mainland where there are plenty of wolves still. As for the Fianna, there traditional range was also in mainland Europe. Most of their Lupus could also come from areas the tribe immigrated to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T10:59:32-08:00","id":1185657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185649#post1185649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could expand the Hakken's kin range to the mainland where there are plenty of wolves still. As for the Fianna, there traditional range was also in mainland Europe. Most of their Lupus could also come from areas the tribe immigrated to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well w20 canonized wolf Cryptids in Japan, which makes a certain amount of sense to me. I mean in a world with changing breeds the various Cryptid Anomolous animals(big cats, wolves still alive in Japan, Thylacines etc) existing because hey a magical human intelligent level version is keeping them protected makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T16:22:14-08:00","id":1185762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185657#post1185657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well w20 canonized wolf Cryptids in Japan, which makes a certain amount of sense to me. I mean in a world with changing breeds the various Cryptid Anomolous animals(big cats, wolves still alive in Japan, Thylacines etc) existing because hey a magical human intelligent level version is keeping them protected makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, from the onset, the WoD wasn't exactly like the real world in demographics. The description laid out that there were fewer small towns and a great deal of untouched wilderness still about to provide the spooky gothic atmosphere. However, the spooky gothic atmosphere is coincidentally also a great place to hide a lot of wild animals that went extinct in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T19:10:23-08:00","id":1185802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1181956#post1181956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: Kitsune<br /> <br /> They are focused as such because they came about in the Hengyokai book during the year of the Lotus late 2nd edition and were not a part of the Werewolf cosmology until then. Any of the Western type Fox-Shifter-Tricksters would be Pooka from Changeling the Dreaming. The Kistune legends have a slightly different flavour to them than the fox legends and myths in the west and as such they worked quite well for the Year of the Lotus to have a different Changing breed from everything done before up to that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, pretty sure the Kitsune first appear in Caerns: Places of Power, along with the Hakken - in fact they get about 10 pages of myth &amp; mechanics in the appendix - back in '93, about half a decade before Hengeyokai and 4 years before there was even a Changeling the Dreaming...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-13-2018, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T20:19:35-08:00","id":1185815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1184660#post1184660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately it doesn\u2019t solve any problem. The Bunyip tribe would have been long extinct for thousands of years before the dingo even showed up.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve no doubt that the original Werewolf writers included the Bunyip/Thylacine thing simply because they saw these things that were sometimes called wolves and decided \u2018this would be cool\u2019. We tried to reconcile that it did exist with why it did so in Shattered Dreams, but you know...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Specifically I think it was the movie Howling III: the Marsupials' fault....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-13-2018, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T20:37:13-08:00","id":1185817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185762#post1185762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, from the onset, the WoD wasn't exactly like the real world in demographics. The description laid out that there were fewer small towns and a great deal of untouched wilderness still about to provide the spooky gothic atmosphere. However, the spooky gothic atmosphere is coincidentally also a great place to hide a lot of wild animals that went extinct in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Its true but I like to try to incorporate &quot;Real&quot; myths even modern stuff like cryptids in my setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T00:07:26-08:00","id":1185842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185649#post1185649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dingo could have arrived to Australia anywhere between 3,500 to 12,000 years ago. Going at the higher end of that range would coincide with the Bunyip's arrival to Australia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the higher end of the range would be 10-20 thousand years later than the Bunyip\u2019s arrival, but no one\u2019s stopping you doing what you want at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T03:54:34-08:00","id":1185871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185842#post1185842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even the higher end of the range would be 10-20 thousand years later than the Bunyip\u2019s arrival, but no one\u2019s stopping you doing what you want at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would certainly fit with the original human settlement of the Americas, that counts as reasonably ancient for garou lore, so more than enough time for a local tribe from dingo stock to shape up. Honestly never saw much sense in considering <i>were-thylacine</i> garou, while prohibiting dog-kinfolk for Bone Gnawers &amp; Glass Walkers. Making them Fera is far more sensible, imho.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185817#post1185817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its true but I like to try to incorporate &quot;Real&quot; myths even modern stuff like cryptids in my setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Drobears? Who's to say they are not what the Bunyip changed into?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-14-2018, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T03:57:44-08:00","id":1185875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185871#post1185871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly never saw much sense in considering <i>were-thylacine</i> garou, while prohibiting dog-kinfolk for Bone Gnawers &amp; Glass Walkers. Making them Fera is far more sensible, imho.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but we work with what we got, and that ain\u2019t what we got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:14:35-08:00","id":1185882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185875#post1185875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but we work with what we got, and that ain\u2019t what we got.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thylacine were called tasmanian wolves, but also tasmanian tigers. Seen anyone proposing they should also be a Bastet (Khan) branch because of that?<br /> <br /> Need i go into the senselessness of Nuwisha/Coyote being Fera while Silent Striders and their jackal stock are garou?<br /> <br /> We work with making the settting our own. Ignore hashly thought fluff, like the lack of perspective/sense of scale of the writers when writing RAA, according to taste.<br /> <br /> Want a compromise solution? Maybe a &quot;dingo bunyip&quot; tribe came to be through adoption/fosterage of lost cubs/foundlings by the &quot;elder bunyip&quot;/<i>were-thylacine</i>, in a kind of variant of how the Children of Gaia came to be from orphans of older tribes being taken aand nurtured by the goddess herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-14-2018, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:18:15-08:00","id":1185883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185882#post1185882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Need i go into the senselessness of Nuwisha/Coyote being Fera while Silent Striders and their jackal stock are garou?<br /> <br /> We work with making the settting our own. Ignore hashly thought fluff, like the lack of perspective/sense of scale of the writers when writing RAA, according to taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be fair they are Jackal looking wolves... just squint!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:32:13-08:00","id":1185888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1181747#post1181747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These were just design choices the original developers made. If you don't like them, change them in your chronicles.<br /> <br /> I never accepted the idea that marsupial predators were wolves, so I've never considered the Bunyip to be Garou. They are simply another Changing Breed. Everything else remain the same - the Garou still wiped them out and then felt guilty about it. I've never had anyone in my games which objected to that.<br /> <br /> In Rage Across Australia, they had Red Talons have the forms of dingoes and in other sourcebooks they've taken the form of Painted Hunting Dogs (in Africa). I've always been leery on this, as once you have Garou assuming non-wolf forms, I think it can create a lot of problems. If Garou can take those forms, why can't Bone Gnawers take the form of at least some dogs?<b> Why are Nuwisha separate from Garou? I think a hard line has to be drawn somewhere so it is coherent, reasonable, and prevents ridiculousness. That line will be different for different people.</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Recent genetic testing has shown that the Coyote diverged from the Grey Wolf only 50,000 years ago and there has been massive interbreeding between coyote and wolf population in the eastern half of the US, especially the south in the last two hundred years. They should not be considered distinct species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:34:59-08:00","id":1185889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185883#post1185883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well to be fair they are Jackal looking wolves... just squint!</div> </div> </div> </div>And with coyotes, &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maned_wolf\" target=\"_blank\">guar\u00e1 wolves</a>&quot; or foxes not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-14-2018, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T04:45:27-08:00","id":1185893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185883#post1185883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well to be fair they are Jackal looking wolves... just squint!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egyptian_wolf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f8/Lupaster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egyptian_wolf\" target=\"_blank\"> Egyptian wolf - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egyptian_wolf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egyptian_wolf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Or they are you know.... actual wolves that were called jackals until fairly recently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T05:38:20-08:00","id":1185907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185893#post1185893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egyptian_wolf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f8/Lupaster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egyptian_wolf\" target=\"_blank\"> Egyptian wolf - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egyptian_wolf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egyptian_wolf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Or they are you know.... actual wolves that were called jackals until fairly recently.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, the Strider breeding doesn't really look like that, it is more this;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/c4/29/90/c4299033905e7fbbb03f601a582f7bf5.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Which makes them look not jackal or wolf-like, but just plain dog-like XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T05:50:46-08:00","id":1185910,"title":"","content":"There's also the mythical and spiritual aspect. In my culture alone wolves, coyotes, and dogs fit very specialized niches in the cosmology. In our stories dogs are considered descended from wolves, but they gave this up when they decided to help guide humans. This transformed them into a new animal and as a result are shunned by the rest.<br /> <br /> Even ignoring Mage's concensuel reality thing, it's in Werewolf canon that reality use to be very different in the past. The Umbra was closer to the physical world, so everything worked far more symbolically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T06:45:35-08:00","id":1185929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185910#post1185910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the mythical and spiritual aspect. In my culture alone wolves, coyotes, and dogs fit very specialized niches in the cosmology. In our stories dogs are considered descended from wolves, but they gave this up when they decided to help guide humans. This transformed them into a new animal and as a result are shunned by the rest.<br /> <br /> Even ignoring Mage's concensuel reality thing, it's in Werewolf canon that reality use to be very different in the past. The Umbra was closer to the physical world, so everything worked far more symbolically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beat me to it. The changing breeds are half spirit and for that reason alone, I am an advocate of the Nuwisha being their own distinct breed. Of we toss the animism and real world cultural inspirations out in in favor of just cold hard science, we miss out on a lot of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T08:32:05-08:00","id":1185964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185842#post1185842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even the higher end of the range would be 10-20 thousand years later than the Bunyip\u2019s arrival, but no one\u2019s stopping you doing what you want at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did the Bunyip come with the Aboriginal migrations to Australia? It's been a while since I read RAA. I just figured they could have came around the time the Dingo arrived.<br /> <br /> There's also the option of what they did to the Ajaba. Gaia could have changed them too from Garou to another breed, keeping them as werethylacines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185888#post1185888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recent genetic testing has shown that the Coyote diverged from the Grey Wolf only 50,000 years ago and there has been massive interbreeding between coyote and wolf population in the eastern half of the US, especially the south in the last two hundred years. They should not be considered distinct species.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is part of the reason why I think Forsaken dropped Lupus. It solves a lot of the problems with these questions from a biological angle if shifters only come from human stock.<br /> <br /> At the same time, to not sound as I'm advocating the erasing of breeds, see my previous post about animals filling different mythical/spiritual niches. It's an angle that often gets forgotten in the pseudo-science parts of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-14-2018, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T12:26:10-08:00","id":1186036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185929#post1185929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beat me to it. The changing breeds are half spirit and for that reason alone, I am an advocate of the Nuwisha being their own distinct breed. Of we toss the animism and real world cultural inspirations out in in favor of just cold hard science, we miss out on a lot of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with this specific call, is that the Garou are not one single werewolf myth. Like most of the WoD games, the PC groups are meant to be expansive and cover a wide variety of mythological inspirations.<br /> <br /> I mean, we have Ragabash trickster werewolves already? We have werewolves that can follow Coyote as a Totem? The idea that we're missing out on something by making coyotes part of the Garou doesn't really seem that... we're missing anything? It just means &quot;trickster coyotes&quot; are a flavor of Garou that doesn't overlap with a flavor of non-Garou Fera. It's not like we can actually make every cultural interpretation of these things work together perfectly anyway.<br /> <br /> It's also kinda jarring when some Fera are restricted to very specific animals (the Kitsune and Nuwisha the most notable) while others are insanely expansive (There are 35K+ species of spiders for the Ananasi to cover). Even in just a half-spirit sense, why are the incredibly disparate Bastet all one group? Qualmi and Simba have... what in common besides being felids? If the Bastet can cover Jaguar inspirations from South America, and Bast inspirations from Egypt, how are the Garou covering the Nuwisha and Kistune as localized groups or whatever removing anything from the game to missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T13:02:21-08:00","id":1186050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1186036#post1186036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem with this specific call, is that the Garou are not one single werewolf myth. Like most of the WoD games, the PC groups are meant to be expansive and cover a wide variety of mythological inspirations.<br /> <br /> I mean, we have Ragabash trickster werewolves already? We have werewolves that can follow Coyote as a Totem? The idea that we're missing out on something by making coyotes part of the Garou doesn't really seem that... we're missing anything? It just means &quot;trickster coyotes&quot; are a flavor of Garou that doesn't overlap with a flavor of non-Garou Fera. It's not like we can actually make every cultural interpretation of these things work together perfectly anyway.<br /> <br /> It's also kinda jarring when some Fera are restricted to very specific animals (the Kitsune and Nuwisha the most notable) while others are insanely expansive (There are 35K+ species of spiders for the Ananasi to cover). Even in just a half-spirit sense, why are the incredibly disparate Bastet all one group? Qualmi and Simba have... what in common besides being felids? If the Bastet can cover Jaguar inspirations from South America, and Bast inspirations from Egypt, how are the Garou covering the Nuwisha and Kistune as localized groups or whatever removing anything from the game to missed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have a point with the Bastet being so widely varied when it comes their tribes or the crazy number of spiders in the world. I guess for me its just a taste issue? I like that the Nuwisha are close enough to Garou that they can infiltrate them, be mistaken as them but are something truly apart. I like that they play by different rules, that they lack Rage and are immune to silver. The fact that superficially and genetically they would be so similar but spiritually are a breed apart. Its the whole looks can be deceiving. I also like that they are there to specifically fill in for those coyote myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T13:34:06-08:00","id":1186056,"title":"","content":"Some of those decision does seem odd, but you can either go with it or ignore them.<br /> <br /> In my WoD I used elements from the &quot;Debased&quot; netbooks for Weredogs. And before the tasmanian tigers, my bunyip, made use of dholes (similar to how the Red Talons are making use of the African Painted Dogs in Africa).<br /> <br /> Not Cannon, but make sense as dhole spread all over Asia from India to Indonesia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T13:49:46-08:00","id":1186060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185907#post1185907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, the Strider breeding doesn't really look like that, it is more this;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/c4/29/90/c4299033905e7fbbb03f601a582f7bf5.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Which makes them look not jackal or wolf-like, but just plain dog-like XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, they don\u2019t really look like real world breeds. Black jackals the size of wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T14:13:50-08:00","id":1186068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1186060#post1186060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly, they don\u2019t really look like real world breeds. Black jackals the size of wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't even look like jackals, since jackal snouts are very petite. They basically look like phraoh hounds that are pitch black. Which fits them looking like anubis, but still doesn't make it any less amusing how doggy some purebred garou are at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T04:29:31-08:00","id":1186239,"title":"","content":"As for artificial restrictions, I do think the Qualmi should not be restricted to North America. The Eurasian Lynx has a vast range even to this day. Sure, say their changers got wiped out west of the Urals, but I think that those east of that in Siberia, Mongolia, China proper and Tibet should have survived. They would make an interesting sorcerous foil to the Kitsune I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T07:57:44-08:00","id":1186308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1186239#post1186239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for artificial restrictions, I do think the Qualmi should not be restricted to North America. The Eurasian Lynx has a vast range even to this day. Sure, say their changers got wiped out west of the Urals, but I think that those east of that in Siberia, Mongolia, China proper and Tibet should have survived. They would make an interesting sorcerous foil to the Kitsune I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Eurasian Quamli was a victim of the War of Rage in cannon, so they have at least been covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T14:26:30-08:00","id":1186415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1186036#post1186036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem with this specific call, is that the Garou are not one single werewolf myth. Like most of the WoD games, the PC groups are meant to be expansive and cover a wide variety of mythological inspirations.<br /> <br /> I mean, we have Ragabash trickster werewolves already? We have werewolves that can follow Coyote as a Totem? The idea that we're missing out on something by making coyotes part of the Garou doesn't really seem that... we're missing anything? It just means &quot;trickster coyotes&quot; are a flavor of Garou that doesn't overlap with a flavor of non-Garou Fera. It's not like we can actually make every cultural interpretation of these things work together perfectly anyway.<br /> <br /> It's also kinda jarring when some Fera are restricted to very specific animals (the Kitsune and Nuwisha the most notable) while others are insanely expansive (There are 35K+ species of spiders for the Ananasi to cover). Even in just a half-spirit sense, why are the incredibly disparate Bastet all one group? Qualmi and Simba have... what in common besides being felids? If the Bastet can cover Jaguar inspirations from South America, and Bast inspirations from Egypt, how are the Garou covering the Nuwisha and Kistune as localized groups or whatever removing anything from the game to missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are wolf and coyote stories and even wolf and Fox stories but there aren't generally mythologically Lion, Tiger and Jaguar stories. That's kind of how I'd split Breeds. So since big cats sort of fit similar setups in different places they'd be united and the small cats might be united as a breed but I'd split bastet in two. I'd also remove all the noncrocadilian Mokole variants.. if you want a wereturtle/lizard/etc it can be its own breed.<br /> <br /> I'm on the fence if Nuwisha should be a Tribe that said &quot;fuck you&quot; or not, like any garou could swear themselves to Coyote.. but then you are a Nuwisha, and have turned away from Luna, I am not sure how it would work but it would be sort of a more extreme tribal break?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T14:48:25-08:00","id":1186422,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit confused by that... there's plenty of mythology around big cats, and even different big cats interacting in areas with significant overlap (mostly Africa, since the rest of the world doesn't have nearly as much territorial sharing between large cats).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T14:51:06-08:00","id":1186425,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of stories for lions, tigers, and jaguars. <br /> <br /> Jaguars are very powerful symbols of royalty, power, war, etc in Mesoamerica and further south. There's some rich tiger stories you can find in Southeast Asia. And for lions, check out the folklore of southeastern Africa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T15:37:56-08:00","id":1186442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1186308#post1186308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the Eurasian Quamli was a victim of the War of Rage in cannon, so they have at least been covered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what happened to them in canon. I'm saying it would be better if they survived in Asia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1186422#post1186422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit confused by that... there's plenty of mythology around big cats, and even different big cats interacting in areas with significant overlap (mostly Africa, since the rest of the world doesn't have nearly as much territorial sharing between large cats).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a modern phenomena. Even well into historic times Lions ranged across all the Mideast, Persia and India. While tigers ranged as far west as the Caspian sea. And of course leopards ranged almost everywhere that lions and tigers did.<br /> <br /> That doesn't even take into consideration the Ice Age when Lions ranged over almost all of Eurasia, North America and parts of South America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":".  Spelling 12-01-2019, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T15:58:22-08:00","id":1186453,"title":"","content":"While big cats used to overlap more, human mythology that Lian was referencing rarely reflects that by having stories about Lion and Tiger go off to do a Thing. We see a lot of mythology around big cats - even in places they haven't been in while in human historical terms - but as far as I understand it the point was that we have fables and stories where Coyote and Wolf, or Fox and Wolf, do a Thing, because they overlapped in area more recently, and thus have more standing as being different kinds of Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T19:40:50-08:00","id":1186523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1186453#post1186453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While big cats used to overlap more, human mythology that Lian was referencing rarely reflects that by having stories about Lion and Tiger go off to do a Thing. We see a lot of mythology around big cats - even in places they haven't been in while in human historical terms - but as far as I understand it the point was that we have fables and stories where Coyote and Wolf, or Fox and Wolf, do a Thing, because they overlapped in area more recently, and thus have more standing as being different kinds of Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. Thus why I am ok with Dingo being Garou because Dingo sort of hit a similar niche as wolves for Australian Natives and they don't have a separate Wolf legend. But the Japanese do have Wolves and Foxes. Native American have Coyote and Wolf and Fox. So I see the point of Nuwisha being a separate thing from Garou.(and Kitsune even more so)<br /> <br /> Jaguar, Lion and Tiger generally don't overlap and.. can interbreed. So I'd be ok with them all being one breed. But for example the Egyptians were sure capable of seeing Cheetah, Lion, and whatever bubastasi are as separate things with different divine connections. So I could see a big cat Fera(Jaguar, Lion, Tiger) a Little cat Fera(Lynx, European Wild Cat, African Wild Cat) and maybe a Medium Cat Breed(I am not so sure on this?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T00:49:29-08:00","id":1186570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1185964#post1185964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the Bunyip come with the Aboriginal migrations to Australia?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, about 10,000 years later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T06:18:19-08:00","id":1186629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1186570#post1186570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, about 10,000 years later.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see the issue then. I thought the Bunyip arrived in Australia around the time the Dingos arrived. I also thought Dingos came with the Aboriginal populations, but Australian history is not my strongest area.<br /> <br /> In my head canon I'd probably have to lean toward they either mystically changed themselves or were changed into werethylacines, or never Garou to begin with if one didn't want to monkey with the timeline. If not it does lead to why the Uktena didn't just mate with South Americas Maned Wolf, let alone the issues raised about Coyotes or other canids across the globe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T12:58:17-08:00","id":1186788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1186629#post1186629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my head canon I'd probably have to lean toward they either mystically changed themselves or were changed into werethylacines, or never Garou to begin with if one didn't want to monkey with the timeline. If not it does lead to why the Uktena didn't just mate with South Americas Maned Wolf, let alone the issues raised about Coyotes or other canids across the globe.</div> </div> </div> </div>With no snark intended, have you read Shattered Dreams? Because it sounds like you\u2019re trying to fix with your head canon what we already went and wrote for you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T14:57:06-08:00","id":1186836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181695-why-is-there-no-dingo-out-of-asia-foxes-out-of-europe-apis-grondr?p=1186629#post1186629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I see the issue then. I thought the Bunyip arrived in Australia around the time the Dingos arrived. I also thought Dingos came with the Aboriginal populations, but Australian history is not my strongest area.<br /> <br /> In my head canon I'd probably have to lean toward they either mystically changed themselves or were changed into werethylacines, or never Garou to begin with if one didn't want to monkey with the timeline. If not it does lead to why the Uktena didn't just mate with South Americas Maned Wolf, let alone the issues raised about Coyotes or other canids across the globe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The first aboriginals arrived in Australia ( unless I've missed some newer findings) about 65,000 years ago....there is still some debate how many waves of aboriginal migration there were but its fairly established that by 40,000 years ago most of the modern language groups were settled into their respective approximate locations. Now as to whether the earlier migrations were driven into Tasmania in much the same way that Thylacines were much later by the relatively recent arrival of dingoes is very much up in the air as far as I know.....not to mention fringe theories like the stories of 'hairy men' being descriptions of remnant communities of earlier hominid migrations.<br /> <br /> Anyway....yeah...Dingoes only rocked up about 10,000 ( some say earlier or later but approx. 10K is fairly settled) years ago after humans....and the Bunyip....had been here a very long time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T01:29:06-08:00","id":1186984,"title":"","content":"I am really inspired for Noah's ark style game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}